 ## Context
 
-The system keeps a veterinary clinic's records. It holds the people who bring animals in, the animals themselves, the appointments those animals attend, and the clinicians the clinic employs. Staff work with it through a browser. They look an owner up by name, then open that owner's record to see every pet and every past appointment. From there they add a pet or book the next visit. A separate page lists the clinic's veterinarians and the specialties they hold.
+The system keeps a veterinary clinic's records. It holds the people who bring animals in, the animals themselves, the appointments those animals attend, and the clinicians the clinic employs. Staff work with it through a browser. They look an owner up by name, then open that owner's record to see every pet and every past appointment. From there they add a pet or book the next visit. A separate page lists the clinic's veterinarians and the specialties they hold. A companion page turns that around, listing each specialty with the veterinarians who hold it.
 
 The domain vocabulary these requirements use — Owner, Pet, PetType, Visit, Veterinarian, Specialty — is defined in [`ubiquitous-language.md`](ubiquitous-language.md).
 
@@ -130,6 +130,22 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the directory the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A specialty directory answers it. It lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under its stored name, with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-VET-003]`. A holder is named in full, first name then last name. Every specialty appears together on one page rather than a page at a time. The page lists specialties rather than the roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears on it nowhere. It is reached directly at its own address rather than through navigation `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed under its stored name on one page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears on the page nowhere.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian named under it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A clinic that knows no specialty is shown an empty directory rather than a failure.
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
